@startuml
' Figure 28-3: TriDemo's three left-hand sides interned into ONE DAG. Compile order
' is rule order (SwapRule, WrapRule, FlipRule); children are interned before parents
' (PatternCompiler::compile, dovetail/src/set_automaton.rs:129). Eleven intern()
' calls produce EIGHT states: FlipRule's Var(x), Var(y), and Pair[s3,s4] all HIT the
' table and return WrapRule's states — s5 is the shared sub-pattern state. SwapRule's
' Var(a)/Var(b) share nothing (the quotient is variable-name-aware). The full trace
' is the table in 28 §6.2; the count is pinned by tridemo_interns_three_rules_into_
' eight_states_sharing_pair (rholang-codegen/tests/doc28_golden_listing.rs).
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName monospaced
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #4A5568
  FontColor #1A202C
}
skinparam ArrowColor #4A5568
top to bottom direction

title Figure 28-3 — TriDemo's interned pattern DAG: 3 rules, 11 raw nodes, 8 states\none shared state s5 = Pair(x,y); RootKey dispatch {Swap,2} {Wrap,1} {Flip,1}

rectangle "entry 0  PatternId(0)\nSwapRule: <latex>\mathrm{Swap}(a,b)</latex>\nFLAT (M1)" as E0 #EDE7F6
rectangle "entry 1  PatternId(1)\nWrapRule: <latex>\mathrm{Wrap}(\mathrm{Pair}(x,y))</latex>\nNESTED (M2)" as E1 #EDE7F6
rectangle "entry 2  PatternId(2)\nFlipRule: <latex>\mathrm{Flip}(\mathrm{Pair}(x,y))</latex>\nNESTED (M2)" as E2 #EDE7F6

rectangle "<latex>s_2 : \mathrm{App}\{\,\mathrm{Swap},[s_0,s_1]\,\}</latex>" as S2 #C3DAF7
rectangle "<latex>s_6 : \mathrm{App}\{\,\mathrm{Wrap},[s_5]\,\}</latex>" as S6 #C3DAF7
rectangle "<latex>s_7 : \mathrm{App}\{\,\mathrm{Flip},[s_5]\,\}</latex>" as S7 #C3DAF7
rectangle "<latex>s_5 : \mathrm{App}\{\,\mathrm{Pair},[s_3,s_4]\,\}</latex>\nSHARED — interned once, hit once" as S5 #9FD3B4
rectangle "<latex>s_0 : \mathrm{Var}(a)</latex>" as S0 #C6E0F5
rectangle "<latex>s_1 : \mathrm{Var}(b)</latex>" as S1 #C6E0F5
rectangle "<latex>s_3 : \mathrm{Var}(x)</latex>\nhit once" as S3 #C6E0F5
rectangle "<latex>s_4 : \mathrm{Var}(y)</latex>\nhit once" as S4 #C6E0F5

E0 -[#805AD5]-> S2 : root_state
E1 -[#805AD5]-> S6 : root_state
E2 -[#805AD5]-> S7 : root_state
S2 -[#2B6CB0]-> S0 : arg 0
S2 -[#2B6CB0]-> S1 : arg 1
S6 -[#2F855A]-> S5 : arg 0
S7 -[#2F855A]-> S5 : arg 0
S5 -[#2B6CB0]-> S3 : arg 0
S5 -[#2B6CB0]-> S4 : arg 1

note right of S5 #FCF3D0
  WrapRule interned Pair(x,y) as s5 (miss);
  FlipRule's compile of the same sub-pattern
  HIT the table and returned s5 — one node,
  two parents. state_count = 8 = 11 − 3 hits.
  Var(a)/Var(b) stay distinct from Var(x)/Var(y):
  the quotient is variable-name-aware (21 §7.1).
end note

legend bottom
  RootKey dispatch (app_roots): {Swap, arity 2} -> [entry 0]   {Wrap, arity 1} -> [entry 1]   {Flip, arity 1} -> [entry 2]
  entry 0 takes the FLAT (M1) serializer path; entries 1 and 2 take the NESTED (M2) descend-then-collapse path (28 §6.3).
endlegend
@enduml
